[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   TEP / Planet-9 -- step b7: is the disk warped with radius?
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   The mean plane of a population is read from its mean orbit pole.
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   A coherent offset of the mean pole from the ecliptic pole is the
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   signature of a shared tilted plane; an offset whose direction or
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   magnitude changes with semimajor axis is a WARP -- the prediction
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   of the inclination-instability picture (Madigan & McCourt) and
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   also of a radially-structured field boundary, but NOT of simple
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   shepherding by a single perturber's plane.
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   The subtlety: the pole azimuth equals Omega - 90 deg, so the
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   measured footprint (nodal discovery bias) imprints a coherent
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   pole offset at EVERY radius even for an unwarped disk.  The
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   calibration must therefore be against the empirical null --
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   control-pool (Om, w) resampling (step b1), which carries the
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   footprint -- not against isotropy.
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   T1  mean pole per a-bin: offset direction (ecliptic longitude
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   of the mean pole) and magnitude (tilt of the mean plane),
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   with the empirical-null band -- is the detached mean pole
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   offset larger than the footprint alone predicts?
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   T2  warp profile: offset magnitude and direction in sliding
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   a-windows -- a coherent drift of the tilt direction with
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   radius is the warp signature.
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   T3  detached vs classical-belt planes: angular separation of the
[2026-09-21 14:31:12 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 018]   two populations' mean poles, bootstrap significance.
